From 3eaf0d9d4a05020805fbcaa63fc388046f5ff140 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 08:08:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): self-heal fix card may requeue the card it
 repaired [daveey]

A worker that fixed a deterministic crash could not return that card to
ready: unblock is orchestrator-only, the shell is fenced, and assignment
routing has no supervisor and is told not to unblock. A self-heal fix card
(created_by=self-heal, key selfheal:<fp>[:rN]:fix) may now unblock the
single card named in its defect. A card that finished fix card created may
do the same, so a completed repair is not stranded. Logged as
self_heal_requeue. The shell fence is unchanged.
---
 hermes_cli/kanban.py                         |  53 ++++
 tests/tools/test_kanban_self_heal_requeue.py | 259 +++++++++++++++++++
 tools/kanban_tools.py                        |  34 +--
 tools/kanban_tools_schemas.py                |   8 +-
 tools/kanban_tools_self_heal.py              |  65 +++++
 5 files changed, 396 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/tools/test_kanban_self_heal_requeue.py
